WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:40.400


00:00:42.647 --> 00:00:46.067
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:00:47.944 --> 00:00:49.028
HIT HOMESHOPPING

00:00:49.112 --> 00:00:51.364
-How many times do I have to tell you?
-Sorry, ma'am.

00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:52.949
-The product is so good!
-Of course!

00:00:53.032 --> 00:00:55.368
Dam Ye-jin's a good seller,
so tell them to get her!

00:00:55.451 --> 00:00:57.537
They said to change them all to big ones.

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:00.874
Coming through.

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:04.377
We're up next after Dam Ye-jin, right?

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.879
Yes, you're up next.

00:01:07.922 --> 00:01:09.090
Hello, ma'am.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.601
-Sir, you have to check this.
-Go do your thing.

00:01:19.684 --> 00:01:20.518
-Thank you.
-Zoom in.

00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:21.686
Okay.

00:01:21.769 --> 00:01:23.646
We're done preparing the samples.

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.481
Hello.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.492
-Hey.
-Yes?

00:01:37.076 --> 00:01:39.787
Is it always a mess like this in studio?

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:41.789
Sorry about that, sir.

00:01:42.332 --> 00:01:43.166
Go.

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:44.083
I'm sorry.

00:01:46.044 --> 00:01:48.671
It's a complete disaster on set.

00:01:50.048 --> 00:01:53.968
Wait, we're about to go live,
but where on earth is Ye-jin?

00:01:56.596 --> 00:01:57.847
Dam Ye-jin's not picking up.

00:01:58.556 --> 00:01:59.641
What?

00:01:59.724 --> 00:02:01.392
What did you just say, Ms. Eom?

00:02:01.476 --> 00:02:02.810
We may have to go on without her.

00:02:02.894 --> 00:02:05.021
How can we go live without the main host?

00:02:05.104 --> 00:02:06.397
I don't know! What do we do?

00:02:07.357 --> 00:02:08.942
All right, everyone.

00:02:09.025 --> 00:02:10.652
The product I'll be introducing today

00:02:10.735 --> 00:02:11.861
is none other than

00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:13.947
all-purpose gloves for cleaning!

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.491
Don't they look as adorable as I do?

00:02:16.574 --> 00:02:17.700
Woof, woof!

00:02:19.869 --> 00:02:21.996
They're 100% made in Korea.
Zero synthetic fibers!

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.289
Perfect for removing stains!

00:02:23.373 --> 00:02:24.374
They're powerful!

00:02:28.086 --> 00:02:30.421
Ms. Eom, let's just roll
a recorded segment right now.

00:02:30.505 --> 00:02:32.882
If something goes wrong on air,
we'll all be done for.

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:34.133
And that's why…

00:02:34.884 --> 00:02:38.012
Sir, we'll go straight into the demo.

00:02:38.096 --> 00:02:41.849
We're not getting many calls,
so how about starting the demo right away?

00:02:42.684 --> 00:02:45.937
Now, I'll demonstrate
the power of these all-purpose gloves.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:46.854
Dust!

00:02:46.938 --> 00:02:50.608
Oh, my God! Jesus!
Now, let's try removing grease!

00:02:54.737 --> 00:02:55.571
All right!

00:02:56.614 --> 00:02:59.117
All right! Okay! Like this!

00:02:59.826 --> 00:03:00.827
Okay!

00:03:02.078 --> 00:03:04.580
Of course, it's hard
to get rid of grease easily.

00:03:05.081 --> 00:03:06.499
You, the floor manager. Come here.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:09.252
All right!

00:03:09.335 --> 00:03:11.337
Hey, why isn't this coming off?

00:03:11.421 --> 00:03:13.673
You're supposed to wet it first.

00:03:13.756 --> 00:03:17.093
All right, our final attack! Hey, grease!

00:03:17.176 --> 00:03:18.011
Take this!

00:03:25.768 --> 00:03:26.978
Hey, are you okay?

00:03:31.149 --> 00:03:32.358
These all-purpose gloves

00:03:32.442 --> 00:03:35.069
may not be that effective,
but aren't they charming?

00:03:36.654 --> 00:03:38.031
We're losing all the calls!

00:03:38.114 --> 00:03:39.365
Please do something, Mr. Hwang!

00:03:39.449 --> 00:03:40.658
Well, let's calm down first.

00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:41.617
"Calm down"?

00:03:42.327 --> 00:03:43.870
Does it look like I can calm down?

00:03:43.953 --> 00:03:45.330
I put my faith in Ms. Dam

00:03:45.413 --> 00:03:48.041
and had everyone work overtime
for an entire month

00:03:48.124 --> 00:03:50.335
to pull together
every bit of stock we could!

00:03:50.418 --> 00:03:53.671
Enough. If today's show flops,
I'm filing a lawsuit right away.

00:03:53.755 --> 00:03:56.257
Ma'am, there's a big problem!

00:03:56.341 --> 00:03:58.134
Our sales are a bigger problem. Look.

00:03:58.217 --> 00:03:59.135
LIVE ORDER STATUS

00:04:00.678 --> 00:04:03.056
Mr. Hwang, you go in
and do the demo instead.

00:04:03.139 --> 00:04:05.892
Tell our host to just talk
and not do anything else.

00:04:05.975 --> 00:04:07.769
What? Me?

00:04:07.852 --> 00:04:08.728
What?

00:04:09.228 --> 00:04:11.230
You can't do it? I guess he can't do it.

00:04:11.314 --> 00:04:13.399
Then, what do we do? I'll go. I can do it.

00:04:13.483 --> 00:04:16.652
Just make quick cuts
and flash the "Almost Sold Out" captions.

00:04:16.736 --> 00:04:18.946
And we'll all take a trip
to the Standards Commission.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:19.989
Move!

00:04:20.073 --> 00:04:22.533
Let go of me!
Let me get on air before they fire me!

00:04:22.617 --> 00:04:24.369
All right, I'll get on standby!

00:04:25.453 --> 00:04:26.704
For crying out loud!

00:04:27.246 --> 00:04:30.458
Who is it? Whose phone is ringing
when we're live…

00:04:35.505 --> 00:04:37.256
Hello?

00:04:38.549 --> 00:04:39.592
Okay, stand by.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:44.764
Action.

00:04:45.348 --> 00:04:47.350
Everyone, were you looking for me?

00:04:47.433 --> 00:04:50.061
I'm greeting you
from a special location today.

00:04:50.144 --> 00:04:52.397
I'm your home shopping host, Dam Ye-jin.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:53.523
Can you guess where I am?

00:04:53.606 --> 00:04:56.776
I'm at the highest building in Korea,

00:04:56.859 --> 00:04:58.361
the Lux Tower.

00:05:02.365 --> 00:05:04.409
Lux Tower!

00:05:04.492 --> 00:05:05.785
-She's finally here.
-Yeah!

00:05:06.869 --> 00:05:08.454
Why am I here?

00:05:08.538 --> 00:05:09.831
Everyone.

00:05:09.914 --> 00:05:11.457
-What?
-Look here.

00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:13.292
-See this window?
-This is incredible.

00:05:13.376 --> 00:05:15.628
This is a year's worth of built-up grime!

00:05:22.218 --> 00:05:23.761
It's crazy, right?

00:05:23.845 --> 00:05:27.306
Ordinary cleaning products
won't be able to remove this.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.475
All right. Watch this.

00:05:30.309 --> 00:05:31.936
I'll spray this cleaner.

00:05:33.438 --> 00:05:34.272
All right.

00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:37.024
Everyone, do you see this?

00:05:37.108 --> 00:05:43.281
I'm wiping pretty hard,
but look at how this grime is still there.

00:05:43.364 --> 00:05:44.198
But now,

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:47.952
I'll show you the power
of these all-purpose gloves.

00:05:50.413 --> 00:05:53.958
All I did was soak these in water,
and I wrung them out.

00:05:54.041 --> 00:05:56.919
You might wonder, "Did she spray them
with bleach or cleaner?"

00:05:59.255 --> 00:06:00.381
How nice and damp.

00:06:00.464 --> 00:06:03.676
Did you see? There's only water on it.
Now, look carefully.

00:06:06.721 --> 00:06:08.389
Where did it all go?

00:06:08.472 --> 00:06:11.934
Everyone, you really have to
try this out for yourself.

00:06:12.018 --> 00:06:13.686
I'm sure you all know what this is.

00:06:13.769 --> 00:06:17.315
Since it lasts even through greasy meals,
they call it "paint lipstick."

00:06:17.398 --> 00:06:20.026
DAM YE-JIN

00:06:20.109 --> 00:06:21.569
Hey, what are you doing?

00:06:21.652 --> 00:06:24.113
Everyone, if I can't erase this,

00:06:24.197 --> 00:06:25.656
I'm going to get in big trouble.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.826
-Will these all-purpose gloves save me?
-Geez, this was expensive!

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:30.578
Just wait and watch.

00:06:30.661 --> 00:06:31.621
All right.

00:06:34.123 --> 00:06:35.917
What do you think?
It's spotless, isn't it?

00:06:36.751 --> 00:06:38.336
That is amazing.

00:06:38.419 --> 00:06:41.505
Everyone, with these all-purpose gloves,
I just got acknowledged

00:06:41.589 --> 00:06:44.634
by a professional building cleaner
with 30 years of experience.

00:06:44.717 --> 00:06:47.136
These gloves will instantly make you
a professional cleaner!

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.223
You'll get a 10% discount
only during this broadcast,

00:06:50.306 --> 00:06:52.892
so place your order now
through our mobile app.

00:06:52.975 --> 00:06:54.644
If I had these, I'd be in the majors.

00:06:54.727 --> 00:06:56.896
Hey, they're not those kinds of gloves!

00:06:56.979 --> 00:06:58.981
Yes, the all-purpose gloves?

00:06:59.065 --> 00:07:02.026
They grab every bit
of dust and grime there is.

00:07:02.735 --> 00:07:05.529
Even fine dust you can't see
is all trapped right in here.

00:07:06.113 --> 00:07:09.408
And it's waterproof inside,
so your hands will stay perfectly dry.

00:07:09.492 --> 00:07:12.578
They're also really easy to clean.

00:07:12.662 --> 00:07:13.871
A large size?

00:07:14.872 --> 00:07:18.543
If you were worried about getting
your hands wet or dirty while cleaning,

00:07:18.626 --> 00:07:20.461
you don't have to worry about that now.

00:07:21.295 --> 00:07:23.256
Do you see how nice and dry my hands are?

00:07:24.048 --> 00:07:25.049
Now,

00:07:25.132 --> 00:07:30.388
let me highlight the key features
of these all-purpose gloves once more.

00:07:30.471 --> 00:07:35.977
Yeah, didn't I tell you?
You can put your faith in Dam Ye-jin.

00:07:38.396 --> 00:07:42.233
Dam Ye-jin really knew what she was doing.

00:07:42.817 --> 00:07:44.944
All right, the second set
is almost sold out as well.

00:07:45.027 --> 00:07:46.529
We're probably going to end early.

00:07:46.612 --> 00:07:47.905
Make sure the next one's ready.

00:07:47.989 --> 00:07:50.658
Everyone, this is going
to be sold out within one minute.

00:07:50.741 --> 00:07:53.578
So hurry.
I'll throw it back to the studio now.

00:07:53.661 --> 00:07:56.122
This has been your host, Dam Ye-jin.
Thank you!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:58.374
Cut!

00:07:59.959 --> 00:08:01.502
I thought I was going to die earlier!

00:08:02.587 --> 00:08:04.255
Wait. Hold on.

00:08:05.047 --> 00:08:06.632
-Hang on. Let me see.
-What is it?

00:08:07.341 --> 00:08:08.175
Just a moment.

00:08:09.677 --> 00:08:11.012
Please…

00:08:12.263 --> 00:08:15.349
We're completely
sold out of today's stock!

00:08:15.433 --> 00:08:16.267
Sold out!

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.689
Everyone, they said we're sold out!

00:08:21.772 --> 00:08:22.607
Sold out?

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:23.691
Sir!

00:08:23.774 --> 00:08:24.775
Sold out!

00:08:24.859 --> 00:08:26.777
-Great job!
-We're sold out!

00:08:27.653 --> 00:08:29.071
Sir!

00:08:31.866 --> 00:08:33.159
-Sold out!
-Sold out!

00:08:35.453 --> 00:08:37.121
Sold out!

00:08:38.497 --> 00:08:40.082
We're sold out!

00:08:41.042 --> 00:08:43.544
Sold out! Thank you!

00:08:43.628 --> 00:08:44.462
Thank you!

00:08:44.545 --> 00:08:51.010
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:09:23.042 --> 00:09:27.046
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

00:09:33.844 --> 00:09:36.013
Mechoori, thank you!

00:09:38.307 --> 00:09:39.308
Sorry?

00:09:39.392 --> 00:09:43.187
Thanks for taking Changsik on a walk.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:45.022
I didn't. He just followed me.

00:09:45.106 --> 00:09:46.190
CHANGSIK
HE DOESN'T BITE

00:09:46.273 --> 00:09:48.776
-And that mutt--
-His name's Changsik.

00:09:49.527 --> 00:09:51.570
Yes, Changsik.
He needs to be put on a leash.

00:09:51.654 --> 00:09:53.864
He'll grow big enough
to high-five you soon.

00:09:53.948 --> 00:09:55.783
What? What's that?

00:09:57.201 --> 00:09:58.494
Well…

00:09:59.995 --> 00:10:01.580
It's like patty-cake…

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.963
Anyway,

00:10:09.046 --> 00:10:11.257
it's dangerous to let him
follow anyone around.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.843
Come on. What do you mean "anyone"?

00:10:13.926 --> 00:10:17.722
Changsik only likes you, Mechoori.

00:10:17.805 --> 00:10:19.640
-He does.
-Whenever he sees you,

00:10:19.724 --> 00:10:21.100
he follows you around!

00:10:21.183 --> 00:10:24.770
-And he follows and follows!
-And he follows and follows!

00:10:25.438 --> 00:10:27.314
I'm not Mechoori.

00:10:27.398 --> 00:10:28.232
What?

00:10:29.316 --> 00:10:30.609
It's Matthew Lee.

00:10:31.652 --> 00:10:33.821
Right. Matthew…

00:10:33.904 --> 00:10:35.740
-Mechoori!
-Mechoori!

00:10:36.741 --> 00:10:37.742
Hey, Mechoori.

00:10:37.825 --> 00:10:39.410
Take these and steam them.

00:10:40.119 --> 00:10:41.746
It's fine. I have a lot of food at home.

00:10:41.829 --> 00:10:43.581
Fine, I'll throw them away.

00:10:43.664 --> 00:10:45.541
Okay, fine.

00:10:45.624 --> 00:10:46.625
You're going to eat them?

00:10:47.585 --> 00:10:49.920
This is too much.
Do you have some for yourself?

00:10:50.004 --> 00:10:52.631
Of course. I have tons left.

00:10:57.136 --> 00:10:58.512
All right. Just this once then.

00:11:01.474 --> 00:11:02.975
Mechoori!

00:11:03.058 --> 00:11:05.644
-Hey, Mechoori!
-Hey. Mechoori!

00:11:05.728 --> 00:11:06.896
Mechoori…

00:11:09.356 --> 00:11:11.066
NO DATA AVAILABLE

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.234
NO INPUT SIGNAL

00:11:12.318 --> 00:11:14.111
See? It's not working.

00:11:14.195 --> 00:11:15.780
The Wi-Fi must be disconnected.

00:11:15.863 --> 00:11:17.114
Why is it so bad?

00:11:17.198 --> 00:11:19.450
Then call your service provider.

00:11:19.533 --> 00:11:21.368
I'll be already dead
by the time they arrive.

00:11:22.328 --> 00:11:23.913
-They'll arrive before that.
-What?

00:11:25.122 --> 00:11:26.832
Mechoori, where are you going?

00:11:26.916 --> 00:11:28.000
Mechoori! Hey!

00:11:30.836 --> 00:11:32.254
Come and sit down.

00:11:33.088 --> 00:11:33.923
Sit down, everyone.

00:11:34.548 --> 00:11:36.967
-Song Ga-in! Song Ga-in!
-Song Ga-in! Song Ga-in!

00:11:37.051 --> 00:11:37.885
Have a seat.

00:11:40.095 --> 00:11:42.097
Are you here to see Song Ga-in too?

00:11:42.598 --> 00:11:44.225
Come and sit down.

00:11:56.237 --> 00:11:57.571
Geez.

00:12:02.535 --> 00:12:03.369
Is it working?

00:12:03.452 --> 00:12:04.453
Go look.

00:12:05.246 --> 00:12:06.830
No!

00:12:06.914 --> 00:12:08.207
Move it to the right.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.583
Just a bit more.

00:12:13.212 --> 00:12:14.421
What about now?

00:12:14.505 --> 00:12:16.340
BEST TROT SINGER
SONG GA-IN

00:12:17.049 --> 00:12:18.425
Just a bit more!

00:12:18.509 --> 00:12:19.802
Just a little more.

00:12:30.938 --> 00:12:32.273
And now?

00:12:34.483 --> 00:12:35.359
It's working!

00:12:35.442 --> 00:12:36.944
It's working now!

00:12:41.699 --> 00:12:43.993
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE SENIOR CENTER OPENING

00:12:47.371 --> 00:12:48.539
Good job!

00:12:48.622 --> 00:12:50.916
-This is awesome!
-It's working really well!

00:12:52.293 --> 00:12:53.294
It looks nice and clear.

00:12:56.922 --> 00:12:59.258
Gosh, thank you so much.

00:12:59.341 --> 00:13:00.593
You can head back now.

00:13:00.676 --> 00:13:02.595
Leave it. I'll put that away.

00:13:02.678 --> 00:13:04.346
It's fine. And one more thing.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.391
That's the last time
I'm going up on the roof.

00:13:07.474 --> 00:13:08.350
Here…

00:13:08.434 --> 00:13:09.602
I'm off.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:16.483
-Mechoori!
-Mechoori!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.243
He's good at driving too.

00:13:29.788 --> 00:13:31.081
Look at him.

00:13:31.165 --> 00:13:31.999
He's so prickly.

00:13:32.082 --> 00:13:34.877
He never says yes with a smile.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.086
That young brat.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.880
Hey, you old brat!

00:13:38.464 --> 00:13:42.134
Even if he speaks curtly,
he's been helping us with everything.

00:13:42.217 --> 00:13:43.969
You shouldn't treat him like that.

00:13:44.053 --> 00:13:45.137
-He's right!
-Yeah!

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:46.347
ONE DAY
AT JONG-IL'S COW SHED

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.848
One, two, three, pull!

00:13:47.931 --> 00:13:49.391
Pull!

00:13:49.475 --> 00:13:52.061
Okay. One, two, three, pull!

00:13:57.024 --> 00:13:58.567
-The teeth look fine.
-That's a relief.

00:13:58.651 --> 00:14:00.277
UNERUPTED TEETH
STILL COVERED BY GUMS

00:14:00.361 --> 00:14:01.779
That was exhausting, wasn't it?

00:14:01.862 --> 00:14:05.449
Mechoori's better than you
at pulling calves now.

00:14:05.532 --> 00:14:06.950
Hey, don't be stupid.

00:14:07.034 --> 00:14:09.787
Don't you know how many calves
I pulled at your shed?

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.206
You don't need to deliver them anymore.

00:14:12.289 --> 00:14:14.541
Mechoori's really come into his own
handling them now!

00:14:14.625 --> 00:14:18.379
Geez, do you know why I'm asking
Mechoori to pull your calves?

00:14:18.462 --> 00:14:23.384
I pity the calves that will have to see
that ugly face of yours their whole lives.

00:14:23.467 --> 00:14:27.179
I wanted to let them
see Mechoori's handsome face for a moment.

00:14:27.262 --> 00:14:28.138
Are you done talking?

00:14:28.222 --> 00:14:29.264
Nope, not at all.

00:14:29.348 --> 00:14:31.850
Have you forgotten
when you used to get beaten up

00:14:31.934 --> 00:14:32.851
all the time?

00:14:32.935 --> 00:14:34.895
Bring it on then. How about a bull fight?

00:14:34.979 --> 00:14:36.188
Go ahead.

00:14:36.271 --> 00:14:37.439
This is my last time

00:14:37.523 --> 00:14:38.941
helping you out in the shed.

00:14:41.777 --> 00:14:43.487
-I'm off.
-Thanks.

00:14:44.488 --> 00:14:46.490
Wait, there's one more!

00:14:46.573 --> 00:14:47.992
Come on! Hurry!

00:14:48.075 --> 00:14:49.118
Come here.

00:14:49.201 --> 00:14:50.911
Damn it.

00:14:52.162 --> 00:14:53.372
That's not all.

00:14:53.455 --> 00:14:55.582
He even chopped all your firewood for you.

00:14:55.666 --> 00:14:59.545
ON ANOTHER DAY,
HOUSE CALL FOR FIREWOOD CHOPPING

00:14:59.628 --> 00:15:00.921
Geez!

00:15:02.047 --> 00:15:03.007
Please…

00:15:04.133 --> 00:15:05.467
He's right!

00:15:05.551 --> 00:15:07.011
And you remember that other time?

00:15:07.594 --> 00:15:11.098
AND ON ANOTHER DAY,
VILLAGE HALL BEEHIVE REMOVAL

00:15:11.181 --> 00:15:12.933
Grab the end. It's okay.

00:15:13.017 --> 00:15:14.601
-Find your balance.
-Don't be scared.

00:15:14.685 --> 00:15:16.603
DEOKPUNG COMMUNITY CENTER

00:15:19.356 --> 00:15:20.441
Yeah, you're right.

00:15:20.524 --> 00:15:23.235
That's right! That day was really fun too.

00:15:24.403 --> 00:15:27.948
AND ON YET ANOTHER DAY,
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE'S KIMCHI-MAKING DAY

00:15:28.032 --> 00:15:30.200
Mechoori, open up.

00:15:33.162 --> 00:15:35.539
"It's Matthew Lee, not Mechoori."

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:37.624
And there's that.

00:15:37.708 --> 00:15:39.460
Why aren't you mentioning that?

00:15:39.543 --> 00:15:41.295
You know. That.

00:15:42.004 --> 00:15:44.798
TYPHOON ROMEO HITS DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

00:15:47.968 --> 00:15:49.970
Oh, come on.

00:15:50.054 --> 00:15:50.929
Damn it.

00:15:52.431 --> 00:15:54.099
And you still think he's prickly?

00:15:55.601 --> 00:15:57.561
I do remember something else.

00:15:57.644 --> 00:15:59.730
Our village might fly away at this rate!

00:15:59.813 --> 00:16:01.356
This is insane.

00:16:01.982 --> 00:16:03.650
Come on. Let's close the window.

00:16:04.318 --> 00:16:06.028
-Close it.
-It's not closing.

00:16:06.612 --> 00:16:11.116
TYPHOON JULIET HITS DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.706
Come on!

00:16:18.332 --> 00:16:19.166
Right!

00:16:19.249 --> 00:16:22.002
We would've been in huge trouble
if it weren't for him.

00:16:22.086 --> 00:16:24.505
-But he wasn't like this from the start.
-Yeah.

00:16:24.588 --> 00:16:26.590
He's finally become a bit nice.

00:16:26.673 --> 00:16:28.342
What did I tell you?

00:16:28.926 --> 00:16:31.595
Mechoori's like streusel bread.

00:16:31.678 --> 00:16:34.890
Rough on the outside
but soft on the inside.

00:16:36.558 --> 00:16:37.559
Streusel bread!

00:16:37.643 --> 00:16:40.354
You're right. Should I go buy
some streusel bread?

00:16:40.437 --> 00:16:42.439
-Sounds nice.
-How many? Two?

00:16:42.523 --> 00:16:44.608
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE BUS STOP

00:16:46.777 --> 00:16:48.195
Mechoori, stop!

00:16:48.278 --> 00:16:50.072
I'm going to get off here!

00:16:55.953 --> 00:16:57.704
Thanks.

00:17:00.457 --> 00:17:02.459
When are you heading back?

00:17:02.543 --> 00:17:04.336
I'm not the village bus driver.

00:17:04.419 --> 00:17:05.921
I'm heading back around 4:30 p.m.

00:17:06.004 --> 00:17:07.506
You can wait for me then or whatever.

00:17:10.551 --> 00:17:11.552
I said 4:30 p.m., okay?

00:17:11.635 --> 00:17:13.512
Okay, 4:30 p.m. See you later.

00:17:16.098 --> 00:17:17.349
Bye.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.785
A simultaneous live broadcast?

00:17:36.869 --> 00:17:38.078
You know how Dam Ye-jin is.

00:17:38.162 --> 00:17:40.247
Once she's set on something,
she stops at nothing.

00:17:40.747 --> 00:17:43.500
My heart was racing,
and I was nervous and anxious all morning.

00:17:43.584 --> 00:17:45.169
I'm filing a workers' comp claim!

00:17:45.252 --> 00:17:46.962
You have to add my name as well.

00:17:47.045 --> 00:17:49.131
The partner company people
threatened to sue me!

00:17:49.214 --> 00:17:52.926
-I really--
-Okay, I get it! You did great.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.678
Hey, it all ended well today.

00:17:54.761 --> 00:17:57.055
You know how intense Dam Ye-jin is.

00:17:59.057 --> 00:18:00.225
But what's with her anyway?

00:18:00.851 --> 00:18:02.895
I know she's popular,
but she's filming commercials…

00:18:02.978 --> 00:18:04.438
WHETHER IT'S RAIN OR SNOW
IONA

00:18:06.315 --> 00:18:07.733
She's a brand ambassador,

00:18:07.816 --> 00:18:10.736
and she's even appearing on Running Man.

00:18:10.819 --> 00:18:12.237
What is she even doing on there?

00:18:12.321 --> 00:18:14.448
What is she going to do? What?

00:18:16.575 --> 00:18:19.328
Superstar Dam! Gosh, no need to be sorry!

00:18:19.411 --> 00:18:20.662
No, it was good!

00:18:20.746 --> 00:18:24.124
Gosh, a true professional
would never complain about that…

00:18:27.002 --> 00:18:28.295
Lunch?

00:18:29.338 --> 00:18:30.172
I'll come by myself.

00:18:30.923 --> 00:18:32.257
Hurry? Okay, I'm coming.

00:18:37.429 --> 00:18:38.263
Are you all right?

00:18:38.847 --> 00:18:40.724
Weren't you even scared?

00:18:40.807 --> 00:18:42.434
Gosh, I'm more afraid of leftover stock.

00:18:42.517 --> 00:18:44.645
I'm late for an engagement,
so I'll get going.

00:18:44.728 --> 00:18:45.687
Ye-jin!

00:18:45.771 --> 00:18:46.980
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:18:47.064 --> 00:18:49.107
-Hello.
-Could we have an autograph?

00:18:49.191 --> 00:18:50.859
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:18:50.943 --> 00:18:52.027
I loved the show.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.363
I'm a huge fan.
Could I get a photo with you?

00:18:54.988 --> 00:18:55.906
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:18:55.989 --> 00:18:57.074
I'm a huge fan.

00:19:15.676 --> 00:19:17.094
Here's your dish.

00:19:17.177 --> 00:19:18.303
Thank you.

00:19:20.764 --> 00:19:22.224
Please enjoy.

00:19:22.307 --> 00:19:23.684
Thank you.

00:19:23.767 --> 00:19:25.978
Lucky you. You always arrive
right when the food comes.

00:19:29.982 --> 00:19:31.108
I'm sorry.

00:19:31.984 --> 00:19:35.404
But I practically
flew over here to see you.

00:19:38.907 --> 00:19:39.741
Eat up.

00:19:45.122 --> 00:19:46.623
Let's watch a movie later.

00:19:46.707 --> 00:19:48.041
We can go after we eat.

00:19:48.125 --> 00:19:49.584
You said you wanted to see this.

00:19:51.461 --> 00:19:52.713
I'm sorry.

00:19:52.796 --> 00:19:55.007
Our new program's launching tomorrow,

00:19:55.966 --> 00:19:58.552
so I have to head back
to work after dinner…

00:20:05.309 --> 00:20:07.352
You know how many surgeries I do each day?

00:20:08.103 --> 00:20:11.857
I'm probably
one of the busiest people in Korea.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:12.983
But "busy" is something…

00:20:13.066 --> 00:20:14.943
What's with this knife? It's light.

00:20:15.027 --> 00:20:16.820
It cuts well. And it's cute.

00:20:16.903 --> 00:20:19.364
This would be nice for a fancy meal.

00:20:19.448 --> 00:20:21.700
Yeah, this is perfect.

00:20:21.783 --> 00:20:23.243
-Are you listening to me?
-You pass.

00:20:23.327 --> 00:20:25.245
I'm sure our customers would love this.

00:20:25.746 --> 00:20:26.830
Should I try to sell it?

00:20:26.913 --> 00:20:28.498
Let's break up.

00:20:33.795 --> 00:20:35.881
Ui-seok, are you angry?

00:20:35.964 --> 00:20:38.050
I'll postpone the meeting.
Let's go see the movie.

00:20:38.133 --> 00:20:42.012
Forget it. You're just going
to keep stepping out to take calls.

00:20:42.095 --> 00:20:43.180
No,

00:20:43.263 --> 00:20:44.431
I'll really--

00:20:44.514 --> 00:20:47.142
Do you really think this is
about me waiting a few minutes?

00:20:48.518 --> 00:20:49.728
What's the matter?

00:20:49.811 --> 00:20:53.774
Aside from surgeries,
I see about 300 outpatients a day too.

00:20:54.649 --> 00:20:57.319
But do you know why
I still make time to date?

00:20:57.402 --> 00:21:00.113
Because I have a personal life.

00:21:00.197 --> 00:21:02.282
I want to live like a human being.

00:21:03.283 --> 00:21:07.746
I just want to laugh
and enjoy my time with you.

00:21:08.872 --> 00:21:12.417
But with you, Dam Ye-jin.
Not home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

00:21:13.377 --> 00:21:14.586
But…

00:21:15.462 --> 00:21:18.215
I can't separate
those two that distinctly.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.806
Then, you can just date that job of yours
that you love so much.

00:21:49.329 --> 00:21:51.289
The gentleman already paid.

00:21:52.165 --> 00:21:54.543
Actually, it's not because of that.

00:21:56.461 --> 00:21:58.004
Your cutlery…

00:21:58.088 --> 00:22:00.465
Could I know who you bought these from?

00:22:07.097 --> 00:22:09.057
Hey, Mr. Hwang.

00:22:10.267 --> 00:22:11.643
Ms. Dam!

00:22:11.726 --> 00:22:13.728
You almost made me faint earlier!

00:22:13.812 --> 00:22:15.647
I… Oh, my gosh!

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:18.900
Mr. Hwang, I found our next product.

00:22:18.984 --> 00:22:21.194
This is cutlery made
from premium stainless steel

00:22:21.278 --> 00:22:22.112
and Nordic wood.

00:22:22.195 --> 00:22:24.156
Both its features
and performance are amazing.

00:22:24.239 --> 00:22:26.825
Let's test it and get in touch
to make it our next product.

00:22:27.451 --> 00:22:28.285
Hang on.

00:22:32.914 --> 00:22:35.584
A Nordic walnut handle
that's been oiled twice

00:22:35.667 --> 00:22:37.919
and intricately carved
to a 1.5mm thickness…

00:22:39.129 --> 00:22:40.630
I can just tell how well it'll cut.

00:22:42.007 --> 00:22:42.841
Let's do it!

00:22:42.924 --> 00:22:44.217
-All right!
-All right!

00:22:48.638 --> 00:22:50.223
Okay. All right, then.

00:22:50.974 --> 00:22:52.142
I'll wait in the lobby.

00:22:52.893 --> 00:22:53.894
Don't be late.

00:23:04.529 --> 00:23:06.448
JI YUN-JI
HIT'S TOP SELLER FOR 2024

00:23:07.282 --> 00:23:09.451
DAM YE-JIN
HIT'S SECOND TOP SELLER FOR 2024

00:23:11.286 --> 00:23:12.829
This business

00:23:12.913 --> 00:23:14.122
is pretty cruel,

00:23:14.206 --> 00:23:15.332
don't you think?

00:23:15.415 --> 00:23:16.541
Sales aren't everything.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.377
But they use photo size
to show the difference.

00:23:21.129 --> 00:23:22.839
I heard you almost made a scene again.

00:23:24.507 --> 00:23:26.009
I actually did.

00:23:26.551 --> 00:23:28.595
We sold 230% of our target.

00:23:28.678 --> 00:23:29.804
That's a huge scene.

00:23:29.888 --> 00:23:32.015
But you're a pro in that area.

00:23:32.098 --> 00:23:35.644
I bring in more with one jar of cream
than you do with ten rags.

00:23:37.395 --> 00:23:38.730
Right.

00:23:38.813 --> 00:23:41.066
While you sell one, I sell ten.

00:23:41.608 --> 00:23:42.776
What?

00:23:42.859 --> 00:23:45.862
Isn't it a relief
that I don't sell cosmetics?

00:23:45.946 --> 00:23:47.405
Look here, Dam Ye-jin.

00:23:51.034 --> 00:23:52.285
Hey.

00:23:52.369 --> 00:23:53.745
We have plans.

00:23:53.828 --> 00:23:54.663
See you later.

00:23:58.583 --> 00:24:00.961
What's the deal with Ji Yun-ji?

00:24:01.044 --> 00:24:03.964
Geez, she's evil to the bone.

00:24:04.047 --> 00:24:06.216
She insults you
instead of being a supportive senior.

00:24:07.217 --> 00:24:08.885
Are you being upset on my behalf?

00:24:08.969 --> 00:24:11.012
Damn it, I've been upset all day!

00:24:11.096 --> 00:24:13.348
If you do that to me again
on a live broadcast,

00:24:13.974 --> 00:24:15.600
regardless of our four-year friendship,

00:24:15.684 --> 00:24:17.060
I'm gone. Got that?

00:24:17.143 --> 00:24:18.728
I got it, so you can stop.

00:24:19.688 --> 00:24:21.856
You don't yell at a woman
who just broke up.

00:24:22.857 --> 00:24:24.985
Why did you get dumped?

00:24:28.238 --> 00:24:30.615
I never said I got dumped.

00:24:31.574 --> 00:24:32.867
I mean…

00:24:34.077 --> 00:24:35.954
-You're so busy.
-So what?

00:24:36.037 --> 00:24:37.455
Everyone's busy.

00:24:37.539 --> 00:24:39.249
But not everyone lives like you.

00:24:39.332 --> 00:24:41.668
How do other people live then?

00:24:43.211 --> 00:24:45.130
You know,

00:24:45.213 --> 00:24:47.716
I work to eat chicken and beer
after clocking out.

00:24:48.425 --> 00:24:50.969
I smile when I think
about chicken and beer,

00:24:51.052 --> 00:24:53.805
and I can endure any crap
that people give me.

00:24:53.888 --> 00:24:56.057
That's what helps me breathe.

00:24:56.141 --> 00:24:57.892
Everyone has something like that.

00:24:57.976 --> 00:25:00.312
A lover, a celebrity they like, a hobby,

00:25:00.895 --> 00:25:02.605
or maybe just a restaurant they like.

00:25:04.482 --> 00:25:06.151
But you?

00:25:06.234 --> 00:25:08.695
You just never clock out of work.

00:25:08.778 --> 00:25:11.197
Well, it just happens
that when I'm working--

00:25:11.281 --> 00:25:13.033
Exactly. So why are you working?

00:25:13.742 --> 00:25:15.452
Don't we all work to live a decent life?

00:25:26.254 --> 00:25:29.174
But do you know why
I still make time to date?

00:25:29.257 --> 00:25:31.676
Because I have a personal life.

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:33.553
I want to live like a human being.

00:25:35.430 --> 00:25:39.893
I just want to laugh
and enjoy my time with you.

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:41.978
But with you, Dam Ye-jin.

00:25:42.896 --> 00:25:44.647
Not home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

00:26:18.807 --> 00:26:21.601
DOESN'T CUT WELL ENOUGH

00:26:31.111 --> 00:26:32.320
PASTEL POPULAR AMONG THE YOUNG

00:27:22.454 --> 00:27:25.081
My daughter, Ye-jin. Your health
is the most important thing.

00:27:25.165 --> 00:27:27.375
No matter how busy you are,
make sure to eat well.

00:27:31.379 --> 00:27:35.175
Hey, I was checking the responses
for the previous Airix product.

00:27:35.258 --> 00:27:36.676
And for the new one, I thought…

00:28:06.372 --> 00:28:07.832
Okay, I'll check that right now.

00:28:08.750 --> 00:28:12.045
Well… Next week…

00:28:12.128 --> 00:28:15.256
I don't think I'll be available next week.

00:28:15.340 --> 00:28:17.425
How about the week after that,
on the 29th?

00:28:18.510 --> 00:28:21.679
I only have one meeting at 3:00 p.m.,
so I can make time in the morning.

00:28:45.620 --> 00:28:46.955
POEMS BY PARK JOON

00:28:50.834 --> 00:28:52.043
That's hot.

00:28:58.216 --> 00:29:00.093
The wavy rubber tip
at the top of the nozzle…

00:29:00.176 --> 00:29:04.347
It's suitable for all hair types,
but especially great for straight hair.

00:29:07.892 --> 00:29:09.394
TAKE ONLY WHEN UNABLE TO SLEEP

00:29:54.230 --> 00:29:57.233
GOJEUNEOK BIO

00:30:02.322 --> 00:30:03.364
Do you

00:30:04.365 --> 00:30:06.618
really want to see me lose it?

00:30:07.911 --> 00:30:09.704
I'm nothing

00:30:09.787 --> 00:30:13.333
without you or money.

00:30:18.004 --> 00:30:19.964
Are you trying to make me the villain?

00:30:20.048 --> 00:30:22.675
-I said I don't need it.
-Just use it, will you?

00:30:25.553 --> 00:30:27.430
So I have to just because you tell me to?

00:30:27.513 --> 00:30:28.431
I won't.

00:30:28.514 --> 00:30:31.225
Just use the new one. It'll be nice
to ride one with a new engine.

00:30:32.018 --> 00:30:33.227
I hate loud things.

00:30:34.687 --> 00:30:37.440
Tractors are supposed to be loud.

00:30:40.401 --> 00:30:41.527
I thought you'd like it.

00:30:43.029 --> 00:30:44.739
I swear, you're so difficult…

00:30:44.822 --> 00:30:47.450
-If that's it, I'm hanging up.
-Wait.

00:30:53.164 --> 00:30:54.749
About that thing…

00:30:56.584 --> 00:30:58.127
So you haven't changed your mind?

00:31:02.674 --> 00:31:04.676
No. Go ahead as planned.

00:31:29.200 --> 00:31:31.494
It's hard covering up
the bags under your eyes today.

00:31:31.577 --> 00:31:33.496
Are you tired?

00:31:33.579 --> 00:31:36.666
No, I'm at full power right now.

00:31:41.587 --> 00:31:44.215
That's Beauty Song's
new product, isn't it?

00:31:44.298 --> 00:31:47.427
Yes, I bought it since it was going viral.

00:31:47.510 --> 00:31:49.971
It's awesome. Just look.

00:31:50.054 --> 00:31:51.556
Your skin looks silky smooth.

00:31:52.140 --> 00:31:53.057
It's good.

00:31:55.018 --> 00:31:56.394
Sir, is this centered?

00:31:56.894 --> 00:31:58.438
-Left? Right? Okay.
-Good.

00:32:03.276 --> 00:32:04.610
Can you place that in the center?

00:32:05.194 --> 00:32:06.404
Hello.

00:32:15.204 --> 00:32:19.542
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1

00:32:21.544 --> 00:32:23.546
EMPLOYEES ONLY

00:32:36.768 --> 00:32:38.186
Hang on.

00:32:38.269 --> 00:32:40.188
You smoke, Mr. Hwang?

00:32:43.191 --> 00:32:44.442
What is it?

00:32:45.234 --> 00:32:46.986
Nervous about your first prime time show?

00:32:48.905 --> 00:32:50.490
-Well…
-I understand.

00:32:51.074 --> 00:32:52.408
Being a merchandiser is tough.

00:32:52.492 --> 00:32:55.244
People say the "MD" in merchandiser
means "must do everything."

00:32:55.870 --> 00:32:57.330
And they say if you're an MD at HIT,

00:32:57.413 --> 00:32:59.457
it means "You're making me crazy,
Dam Ye-jin."

00:33:01.751 --> 00:33:03.753
Spill it! What's the matter?

00:33:14.138 --> 00:33:15.765
WEEKLY BROADCAST SCHEDULE

00:33:15.848 --> 00:33:17.100
THE JI YUN-JI SHOW

00:33:17.183 --> 00:33:18.434
Damn it!

00:33:19.936 --> 00:33:24.649
How about changing the background color
to violet like the brand's color?

00:33:24.732 --> 00:33:25.566
Violet?

00:33:25.650 --> 00:33:27.360
And…

00:33:27.443 --> 00:33:30.947
The light might reflect off the products,
so please check the angles.

00:33:32.323 --> 00:33:33.157
Ma'am?

00:33:34.367 --> 00:33:36.035
Well…

00:33:42.375 --> 00:33:44.418
Did you get the studios wrong?

00:33:44.502 --> 00:33:46.420
This is the Saturday prime time studio.

00:33:47.547 --> 00:33:49.882
I guess you haven't seen
the changed schedule.

00:33:49.966 --> 00:33:52.635
Tonight's prime time slot
has changed to The Ji Yun-ji Show.

00:33:52.718 --> 00:33:54.637
We're launching Beauty Song's compact.

00:33:56.013 --> 00:33:57.098
Beauty Song?

00:33:57.765 --> 00:33:58.599
Yeah.

00:34:16.742 --> 00:34:18.786
It seems the set hasn't been cleared yet.

00:34:19.453 --> 00:34:21.330
Ms. Song.

00:34:21.414 --> 00:34:24.959
Ms. Dam didn't see the updated schedule.

00:34:25.626 --> 00:34:26.752
Oh, my.

00:34:26.836 --> 00:34:29.547
You really haven't changed, Ms. Dam.

00:34:38.556 --> 00:34:39.807
Aren't you sick

00:34:39.891 --> 00:34:42.185
of saying "I didn't know" as an excuse?

00:34:44.228 --> 00:34:47.440
-Everyone, I think we should hurry.
-Yes, ma'am.

00:34:50.860 --> 00:34:52.320
-Let's take all these out.
-One, two!

00:34:53.613 --> 00:34:55.323
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1

00:34:55.406 --> 00:34:56.782
I'm sorry.

00:34:58.367 --> 00:34:59.452
Okay, let's proceed.

00:35:07.460 --> 00:35:09.253
MAKING ME CRAZY DAM YE-JIN

00:35:18.596 --> 00:35:20.640
ANSWER WITHIN TEN SECONDS

00:35:20.723 --> 00:35:22.350
Don't answer. It'll be a disaster.

00:35:22.433 --> 00:35:25.394
-Should I turn it off?
-No, that would be worse.

00:35:25.937 --> 00:35:28.231
She wouldn't go straight
to the director, would she?

00:35:28.773 --> 00:35:30.983
Come on. Even if she's practically
a human bulldozer,

00:35:31.067 --> 00:35:33.069
she'd be insane to just barge in there.

00:35:33.152 --> 00:35:34.237
Right?

00:35:45.164 --> 00:35:46.874
I didn't hear you knock.

00:35:46.958 --> 00:35:49.460
You're the one who skipped protocol first.

00:35:49.543 --> 00:35:51.921
Why was the schedule changed
to The Ji Yun-ji Show?

00:35:52.004 --> 00:35:54.215
How could you do this
without even telling me?

00:35:57.510 --> 00:35:59.053
At this rate,

00:35:59.136 --> 00:36:01.639
we'll be crushed by CT Life Shopping
before the next quarter.

00:36:01.722 --> 00:36:04.308
Beauty Song's Song Myeong-hwa Compact

00:36:04.392 --> 00:36:06.269
was the one that boosted CT's sales.

00:36:06.352 --> 00:36:07.436
So if they're coming to us,

00:36:07.520 --> 00:36:09.855
shouldn't we offer
our prime time slot on Saturday?

00:36:09.939 --> 00:36:11.524
Why does it have to be my slot?

00:36:11.607 --> 00:36:12.858
The prime time slot

00:36:12.942 --> 00:36:14.777
is for best-selling products,

00:36:14.860 --> 00:36:16.821
not for hosts who have good sales.

00:36:18.656 --> 00:36:21.826
You know that beauty products
are the real moneymakers.

00:36:21.909 --> 00:36:22.743
Ma'am,

00:36:22.827 --> 00:36:27.331
our team's average target achievement rate
for the past three months is over 180%.

00:36:27.415 --> 00:36:29.417
And with prime time consumers,

00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:31.294
we'll be able to show even better results…

00:36:32.628 --> 00:36:33.754
That's right.

00:36:33.838 --> 00:36:36.465
It's the brand that both
Haeseong Duty Free and Lux Duty Free

00:36:37.300 --> 00:36:40.219
were desperate to get on board

00:36:40.303 --> 00:36:41.929
but failed to in the end.

00:36:43.431 --> 00:36:44.515
L'Étoile.

00:36:45.599 --> 00:36:48.227
We'll need a brand like that
to push out Beauty Song.

00:36:48.769 --> 00:36:50.146
I don't sell cosmetics.

00:36:51.856 --> 00:36:54.692
That clause has always
been in my contracts.

00:36:55.568 --> 00:36:56.736
But I guess you forgot.

00:36:57.570 --> 00:36:59.989
I'll find a product
that is as good as L'Étoile's.

00:37:00.072 --> 00:37:02.116
The Danish royal tableware
you mentioned before--

00:37:02.199 --> 00:37:04.744
You seem mistaken about something.

00:37:04.827 --> 00:37:06.996
But L'Étoile is the only brand

00:37:07.580 --> 00:37:10.166
that would allow you
to retake the prime time slot.

00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:12.376
If you can't do that,

00:37:12.460 --> 00:37:15.963
then your dream of hosting a show
with your name on it will end here.

00:37:16.047 --> 00:37:18.674
-Ma'am!
-When are you going to stop running away?

00:37:20.593 --> 00:37:22.094
Are you going to betray

00:37:22.178 --> 00:37:25.556
the partner companies, merchandisers,
and producers relying on you over this?

00:37:28.392 --> 00:37:30.186
The next time you enter my office,

00:37:30.269 --> 00:37:32.480
you'd better have
a contract with L'Étoile.

00:37:42.073 --> 00:37:42.907
Ms. Dam.

00:37:43.407 --> 00:37:44.408
Have you lost your mind?

00:37:44.492 --> 00:37:46.160
How could you barge in there like that?

00:37:46.243 --> 00:37:47.787
So what did the director say?

00:37:48.704 --> 00:37:50.873
What is it? What did she say?

00:37:50.956 --> 00:37:52.917
She said that if I want my spot back,

00:37:54.168 --> 00:37:55.961
I have to bring L'Étoile on board.

00:37:57.046 --> 00:37:58.339
-L'Étoile?
-What?

00:37:58.422 --> 00:38:00.257
You mean the French brand, L'Étoile?

00:38:01.092 --> 00:38:02.927
But Ms. Dam doesn't do cosmetics.

00:38:05.054 --> 00:38:06.180
That hurts.

00:38:07.348 --> 00:38:10.101
Damn it. How can Ms. Dong be so cruel?

00:38:10.184 --> 00:38:11.185
Wait!

00:38:11.268 --> 00:38:13.354
How in the world
is she going to bring in L'Étoile?

00:38:13.437 --> 00:38:14.438
I know.

00:38:46.679 --> 00:38:49.223
It's not like I'm a celebrity or anything.

00:38:49.306 --> 00:38:52.059
If word gets out that you're in Korea,

00:38:52.143 --> 00:38:55.896
the duty-free retailers
who sent in offers will be all over you.

00:38:55.980 --> 00:38:58.941
Then, our confidential information
would be exposed in no time.

00:38:59.024 --> 00:39:01.652
Look, no one in Korea would recognize me…

00:39:05.281 --> 00:39:06.490
Where are we going?

00:39:06.574 --> 00:39:08.492
What's trending in Korea these days?

00:39:08.576 --> 00:39:10.911
First, let me take you to your hotel.

00:39:10.995 --> 00:39:14.290
You can rest there
until your evening meeting.

00:39:15.416 --> 00:39:16.750
You don't mean tonight, do you?

00:39:17.460 --> 00:39:18.586
I do, sir.

00:39:18.669 --> 00:39:20.504
But I just got here from France.

00:39:20.588 --> 00:39:22.465
Well, the meeting
is what you came here for.

00:39:26.093 --> 00:39:29.138
Did you say the raw material supplier
was called Gojeuneok Bio?

00:39:30.014 --> 00:39:30.848
Yes.

00:39:44.862 --> 00:39:48.240
It's nice to meet you.
I'm Kang Mu-won, CEO of Gojeuneok Bio.

00:39:48.324 --> 00:39:51.035
Hello. I'm Eric Seo,
Executive Director at L'Étoile.

00:39:51.118 --> 00:39:52.745
Nice to meet you. Please take a seat.

00:39:53.579 --> 00:39:57.166
We offered very favorable terms
in the new raw material supply contract.

00:39:57.249 --> 00:39:58.709
Have you considered it?

00:39:58.792 --> 00:40:00.085
CONTRACT AMENDMENT PROPOSAL

00:40:06.634 --> 00:40:10.179
Of course. I considered it very carefully.

00:40:11.096 --> 00:40:11.931
Then--

00:40:12.014 --> 00:40:13.933
But I won't be able to give
the answer you want.

00:40:14.016 --> 00:40:16.101
I'm sorry you had to come all this way.

00:40:17.061 --> 00:40:18.395
To be honest,

00:40:18.479 --> 00:40:20.272
this is hard to understand.

00:40:20.356 --> 00:40:23.067
We increased
the previous order volume by five times,

00:40:23.150 --> 00:40:26.820
and we also adjusted the terms to be
much more favorable to Gojeuneok Bio.

00:40:28.656 --> 00:40:30.991
You're worried you won't be able to manage

00:40:31.075 --> 00:40:32.576
-the increased volume, right?
-Yes.

00:40:32.660 --> 00:40:35.412
Yes, I think that seems
to be the biggest concern…

00:40:38.040 --> 00:40:39.625
I mean, it is the biggest concern.

00:40:41.335 --> 00:40:42.336
Then,

00:40:42.419 --> 00:40:45.172
we'll come up with a way
to resolve that issue.

00:40:45.256 --> 00:40:46.090
No,

00:40:46.173 --> 00:40:47.758
let me be clear about this.

00:40:47.841 --> 00:40:48.801
Gojeuneok Bio

00:40:49.677 --> 00:40:51.804
will not renew our contract with L'Étoile.

00:41:06.694 --> 00:41:09.697
You must be tired.
Should I take you back to the hotel?

00:41:09.780 --> 00:41:10.990
Mr. Cha.

00:41:11.699 --> 00:41:14.285
There's something strange about Mr. Kang.

00:41:14.910 --> 00:41:16.912
It was like he was speaking
for someone else.

00:41:17.454 --> 00:41:21.083
Then I'll look into Gojeuneok Bio
a bit more.

00:41:23.627 --> 00:41:27.089
My sister must be worried sick
that I'm slacking off here.

00:41:27.172 --> 00:41:31.719
Our deputy CEO, Michelle,
is especially worried about you.

00:41:34.346 --> 00:41:35.764
Oh, dear. It's raining.

00:41:38.726 --> 00:41:40.477
We should get this done quickly

00:41:40.978 --> 00:41:42.062
before it's too late.

00:41:42.980 --> 00:41:44.732
The first set has sold out.

00:41:44.815 --> 00:41:45.816
Oh, my!

00:41:45.899 --> 00:41:47.943
It's sold out. My gosh!

00:41:48.527 --> 00:41:49.945
It's already sold out.

00:41:50.029 --> 00:41:54.491
You know, it's only been 30 minutes
since we started the show.

00:41:54.575 --> 00:41:58.370
We have an hour,
but it's already sold out. At this rate…

00:41:58.454 --> 00:41:59.788
All right!

00:41:59.872 --> 00:42:02.333
Since it's late,
how about a late-night snack--

00:42:02.416 --> 00:42:04.793
What? So we can watch her show?

00:42:04.877 --> 00:42:06.420
What do we do with our remaining time?

00:42:06.503 --> 00:42:08.839
Why isn't this turning off? Damn it!

00:42:08.922 --> 00:42:10.591
I am so surprised too.

00:42:15.179 --> 00:42:16.388
Just go home now.

00:42:16.472 --> 00:42:17.556
Right.

00:42:17.640 --> 00:42:19.141
I don't even want to be

00:42:19.224 --> 00:42:21.101
in the same building
as Ji Yun-ji right now.

00:42:23.771 --> 00:42:24.605
Get up.

00:42:35.824 --> 00:42:37.493
What's really surprising is

00:42:37.576 --> 00:42:40.412
that blotting paper
doesn't seem to stick to this at all.

00:42:40.496 --> 00:42:42.331
-Right.
-If I put a sheet

00:42:42.414 --> 00:42:43.666
of blotting paper on my face…

00:42:43.749 --> 00:42:45.042
Look. Seriously.

00:42:45.125 --> 00:42:47.294
It just falls off right away.

00:42:48.545 --> 00:42:50.547
ACTRESS SONG MYEONG-HWA'S
BEAUTY SONG COMPACT

00:43:13.779 --> 00:43:15.781
-We demand compensation!
-We demand compensation!

00:43:15.864 --> 00:43:16.824
WE SUFFER EVERY DAY

00:43:21.328 --> 00:43:24.039
I'm sorry. I apologize.

00:43:24.832 --> 00:43:26.333
My skin feels so moist.

00:43:26.417 --> 00:43:29.753
I gave away all of my blotting paper
to my friends and acquaintances.

00:43:29.837 --> 00:43:31.463
-Really?
-Yes, seriously.

00:43:31.547 --> 00:43:32.631
I see.

00:43:32.715 --> 00:43:35.592
As time passes by,

00:43:35.676 --> 00:43:39.054
we want to make our skin smooth
and gentle.

00:43:39.138 --> 00:43:41.515
When you get to your forties,
fifties, and sixties…

00:44:08.959 --> 00:44:10.544
Stick with your usual size.

00:44:11.336 --> 00:44:13.756
Customer 8782 is asking about washing it.

00:45:20.656 --> 00:45:23.450
That's why we prepared
oil directly imported from Italy.

00:45:24.785 --> 00:45:26.495
Even if you put it in the washing machine…

00:45:28.622 --> 00:45:30.249
I'll discuss it with them right away.

00:45:30.332 --> 00:45:32.918
The lineup is made up of these three…

00:45:54.147 --> 00:45:57.317
Ms. Dam, you've already hit
the maximum dose and duration.

00:45:57.401 --> 00:45:59.945
If you keep overusing sleeping pills,

00:46:00.028 --> 00:46:02.030
you may experience serious side effects,

00:46:02.114 --> 00:46:05.284
such as sleepwalking, memory loss,
and even respiratory depression.

00:46:05.367 --> 00:46:07.828
You could seriously hurt yourself.

00:46:10.747 --> 00:46:12.916
Just one pill per day.
Please stick to that.

00:46:18.130 --> 00:46:19.756
When are you going to stop running away?

00:46:19.840 --> 00:46:22.134
Aren't you sick
of saying "I didn't know" as an excuse?

00:46:28.599 --> 00:46:29.600
We'll get ready now!

00:46:29.683 --> 00:46:31.685
-Excuse me.
-Don't step on that!

00:46:31.768 --> 00:46:32.936
Out of the way!

00:46:33.562 --> 00:46:34.605
Please take this out too.

00:46:34.688 --> 00:46:36.064
-Passing through.
-Excuse me.

00:46:36.773 --> 00:46:38.025
Ms. Dam?

00:46:38.108 --> 00:46:39.860
We're starting now. There's no time.

00:47:32.245 --> 00:47:36.124
MS. ANGRY EOM

00:47:42.464 --> 00:47:45.050
Ms. Eom, is it another
simultaneous live broadcast today?

00:47:45.133 --> 00:47:48.095
Why isn't she picking up her phone again?

00:47:49.012 --> 00:47:51.598
Is she not here yet?

00:47:52.182 --> 00:47:54.309
This won't do.
I'll look for a recorded segment.

00:47:54.393 --> 00:47:56.812
You try to do something here.

00:47:56.895 --> 00:47:57.979
-Do what?
-Anything.

00:47:58.063 --> 00:47:59.856
-Just do something.
-What…

00:47:59.940 --> 00:48:01.358
Hey! You little…

00:48:01.441 --> 00:48:03.026
-Sorry.
-Geez.

00:48:03.110 --> 00:48:04.361
What's wrong? Are you sick?

00:48:04.444 --> 00:48:05.570
Sorry, I'll go get ready.

00:48:05.654 --> 00:48:07.656
Hang on. Is something wrong?

00:48:08.198 --> 00:48:09.032
I'm fine.

00:48:09.116 --> 00:48:10.492
For crying out loud.

00:48:10.575 --> 00:48:12.285
I'm really okay.

00:48:13.829 --> 00:48:16.498
We hope all your days
are healthy days with Binox.

00:48:16.581 --> 00:48:18.583
Thank you for all of your love
and support today.

00:48:18.667 --> 00:48:21.503
This was your home shopping host,
Dam Ye-jin. Thank you.

00:48:23.964 --> 00:48:25.006
Great job!

00:48:31.221 --> 00:48:32.723
You can't focus on just the symptoms.

00:48:32.806 --> 00:48:34.474
Real issues and relationships

00:48:34.558 --> 00:48:36.226
that you can't avoid are connected to it.

00:48:36.977 --> 00:48:39.396
There are underlying factors
behind your insomnia.

00:48:40.230 --> 00:48:43.817
To break this nightly cycle of insomnia,

00:48:43.900 --> 00:48:46.111
you have to resolve the root cause first.

00:48:47.529 --> 00:48:49.489
-Goodbye!
-Bye!

00:48:49.573 --> 00:48:51.199
It's time to face it now.

00:48:52.242 --> 00:48:53.785
You must figure out

00:48:54.411 --> 00:48:56.872
what is deep down inside
that's pulling you down.

00:48:58.081 --> 00:48:59.332
Hey, don't joke around.

00:48:59.416 --> 00:49:01.084
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

00:49:01.168 --> 00:49:02.753
Get home safely.

00:49:08.300 --> 00:49:10.260
Mechoori!

00:49:15.932 --> 00:49:17.476
-Did you have a good day?
-Yeah.

00:49:18.643 --> 00:49:19.811
Thanks.

00:49:48.006 --> 00:49:49.466
-What's this?
-Striped maple extract.

00:49:50.217 --> 00:49:51.968
I knew you'd never drink it if I told you.

00:49:53.637 --> 00:49:55.263
I saw you vomiting.

00:49:56.306 --> 00:49:57.766
So don't complain and just drink it.

00:49:57.849 --> 00:49:59.810
It helps with stress-related gastritis.

00:50:06.942 --> 00:50:07.943
I really can't drink it.

00:50:09.444 --> 00:50:12.197
You don't have to bring in L'Étoile
if you don't want to.

00:50:13.114 --> 00:50:14.991
What about our team if I don't?

00:50:17.786 --> 00:50:21.540
If we get fired, we can just go to CT.

00:50:22.082 --> 00:50:23.917
Hey, after spending four years

00:50:24.000 --> 00:50:26.545
working with someone
who sells everything besides cosmetics,

00:50:26.628 --> 00:50:28.964
I have experience
in every field except makeup.

00:50:29.047 --> 00:50:31.550
You could say I'm an all-rounder.

00:50:36.680 --> 00:50:37.681
Do you know what this is?

00:50:45.730 --> 00:50:48.441
Four years ago, after our first show,

00:50:48.525 --> 00:50:51.361
you left this product description
behind in the studio.

00:50:51.945 --> 00:50:54.823
I think we reached
only about 30% of our target rate.

00:50:54.906 --> 00:50:57.701
Remember how we totally messed up?

00:50:57.784 --> 00:51:00.078
I wondered if it was a mistake
working with you,

00:51:00.161 --> 00:51:02.581
but the moment I saw that,
I felt relieved.

00:51:03.373 --> 00:51:06.001
I knew if you were this dedicated,
I could trust you.

00:51:07.335 --> 00:51:08.920
But now,

00:51:09.004 --> 00:51:12.299
you sell over 200% of our target rates.

00:51:12.382 --> 00:51:14.092
Seriously, aren't you proud?

00:51:14.968 --> 00:51:16.344
What are you trying to say?

00:51:17.220 --> 00:51:19.514
There are a lot of people
who trust you now.

00:51:20.056 --> 00:51:23.184
So you should trust yourself too.

00:52:04.184 --> 00:52:06.269
There's still so much left.

00:52:11.149 --> 00:52:12.317
That's my sister, right?

00:52:13.443 --> 00:52:14.277
No, it isn't.

00:52:16.029 --> 00:52:18.406
I'm not sure if you've heard,

00:52:18.490 --> 00:52:21.451
but the biggest home shopping company
in Korea is called HIT.

00:52:21.534 --> 00:52:24.454
It's been consistently
sending in offers since last year.

00:52:25.163 --> 00:52:26.998
I know HIT. They contacted you?

00:52:27.082 --> 00:52:29.376
Yes, it's a host named Dam Ye-jin…

00:52:30.168 --> 00:52:31.169
Who?

00:52:32.379 --> 00:52:34.339
Home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

00:52:34.422 --> 00:52:38.259
It seems like HIT found out
that you're in Korea.

00:52:38.343 --> 00:52:40.804
-She's asking for a meeting.
-Set it up as soon as possible.

00:52:40.887 --> 00:52:45.225
What? But, sir, we still have to deal
with the renewal contract--

00:52:45.308 --> 00:52:48.436
Mr. Cha, I've been stuck here
looking at papers for a whole week.

00:52:48.520 --> 00:52:51.398
Don't you understand how desperate I am

00:52:51.481 --> 00:52:53.316
to just talk to someone?

00:52:53.984 --> 00:52:54.985
Don't you?

00:53:16.172 --> 00:53:17.382
Hi…

00:53:19.092 --> 00:53:20.635
I mean, hello.

00:53:20.719 --> 00:53:23.638
Nice to meet you.
I'm home shopping host Dam Ye-jin.

00:53:27.142 --> 00:53:28.893
Nice to meet you.

00:53:48.288 --> 00:53:49.748
I like the proposal.

00:53:50.957 --> 00:53:53.084
Did you read through it carefully?

00:53:53.168 --> 00:53:56.379
Of course. You did too, right?

00:53:56.921 --> 00:54:00.884
Our meeting was scheduled in a hurry,
so you could've missed something.

00:54:01.718 --> 00:54:04.095
Please take another good look.

00:54:12.562 --> 00:54:15.899
I've already reviewed it thoroughly.

00:54:22.155 --> 00:54:24.783
We'll review your proposal
with a positive outlook.

00:54:28.286 --> 00:54:33.083
I actually didn't expect our meeting
to go so smoothly like this.

00:54:33.625 --> 00:54:37.087
I believe HIT has been sending offers
to L'Étoile since last year.

00:54:37.670 --> 00:54:39.172
So could I ask the reason for this?

00:54:40.131 --> 00:54:43.301
Well, we also have one condition.

00:54:51.476 --> 00:54:52.644
So, you're saying

00:54:52.727 --> 00:54:56.648
we have to work with you to resolve
your raw material renewal contract?

00:54:56.731 --> 00:54:59.692
Yes. If you can help us
resolve this matter,

00:54:59.776 --> 00:55:01.402
then I'll prioritize HIT's offer

00:55:01.486 --> 00:55:03.488
as soon as I return to France.

00:55:05.615 --> 00:55:08.701
Then, I'll take responsibility
and solve this matter.

00:55:08.785 --> 00:55:10.620
You're accepting my proposal?

00:55:11.746 --> 00:55:13.832
Yes, if you promise
to come on board right now.

00:55:16.626 --> 00:55:18.378
I don't have much time either.

00:55:19.838 --> 00:55:22.882
Since we don't have much time,
why don't we proceed on two fronts?

00:55:22.966 --> 00:55:25.426
You focus on convincing
the CEO of Gojeuneok Bio,

00:55:25.510 --> 00:55:27.887
and I'll focus on convincing
the raw material farm owner.

00:55:27.971 --> 00:55:29.639
The farm owner? Why?

00:55:29.722 --> 00:55:32.809
Gojeuneok Bio cultivates
their own raw materials.

00:55:33.393 --> 00:55:36.938
If we get the farm owner on our side,
we'll have a better advantage negotiating.

00:55:37.856 --> 00:55:39.357
By the way…

00:55:40.984 --> 00:55:43.736
Should we officially exchange numbers now?

00:55:44.654 --> 00:55:45.697
Sure.

00:55:51.035 --> 00:55:52.078
Here.

00:56:18.521 --> 00:56:19.772
Gosh, my feet.

00:56:23.860 --> 00:56:25.111
Let's rest a bit.

00:56:28.239 --> 00:56:29.199
Oh, my gosh.

00:56:30.909 --> 00:56:31.910
Hey, perfect timing.

00:56:31.993 --> 00:56:35.330
Hello, Su-min.
Give me a ride to the living room.

00:56:35.413 --> 00:56:36.706
Pardon?

00:56:37.290 --> 00:56:39.000
-Hey, why are you turning around?
-Pardon?

00:56:39.083 --> 00:56:40.668
-Hey!
-Pardon?

00:56:40.752 --> 00:56:42.170
Hey, Su-min… Hello, Su-min!

00:56:42.253 --> 00:56:43.296
-Come here.
-Pardon?

00:56:43.379 --> 00:56:44.589
-Hello--
-My name is Su-min.

00:56:44.672 --> 00:56:46.966
-Hey, Su-min. Come back here.
-I am not able to do that.

00:56:47.050 --> 00:56:48.301
Hey, where are you going?

00:56:48.384 --> 00:56:49.719
My name is Su-min.

00:56:49.802 --> 00:56:51.179
Fine. Just go.

00:56:51.262 --> 00:56:52.180
Pardon?

00:56:52.263 --> 00:56:53.223
You're out.

00:56:53.306 --> 00:56:54.641
I do not understand.

00:56:56.226 --> 00:56:57.518
What am I doing?

00:56:58.144 --> 00:57:00.647
-I do not understand what you are saying.
-Be quiet.

00:57:18.373 --> 00:57:20.083
L'Étoile.

00:57:28.841 --> 00:57:31.219
Let's see.

00:57:40.520 --> 00:57:44.649
The key ingredient of the essence
seems to be WF-Mushroom.

00:57:44.732 --> 00:57:46.484
Find more data on this.

00:57:46.568 --> 00:57:50.071
WF-Mushroom is the key ingredient
in La Fin Essence

00:57:50.154 --> 00:57:53.324
and makes up over 90% of the formula.

00:57:53.408 --> 00:57:55.910
It's an extract
of the white flower noori mushroom.

00:57:57.287 --> 00:57:59.914
Can you explain more
about the white flower noori mushroom?

00:57:59.998 --> 00:58:02.375
The white flower noori mushroom
is native to Korea,

00:58:03.126 --> 00:58:05.878
and its extract is known
for boosting skin elasticity,

00:58:05.962 --> 00:58:08.965
reducing pore size,
and providing antioxidant benefits.

00:58:10.300 --> 00:58:12.260
I like the data.

00:58:12.343 --> 00:58:14.387
You're useful. You get a pass.

00:58:29.485 --> 00:58:31.529
HIT HOMESHOPPING

00:58:36.492 --> 00:58:37.577
All done.

00:59:06.147 --> 00:59:07.857
You're heading to the farm?

00:59:07.940 --> 00:59:10.068
Yes, I wanted to check it myself.

00:59:10.735 --> 00:59:12.111
What's the exact address?

00:59:13.112 --> 00:59:15.448
We only know
that it's in Deokpung Village.

00:59:18.034 --> 00:59:19.661
Then, I'll just go and ask around.

00:59:20.244 --> 00:59:22.246
There can't be many farms
that big in the country.

00:59:50.942 --> 00:59:53.736
From here, go straight.

00:59:59.075 --> 01:00:02.370
GOODBYE
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE EXIT

01:00:13.881 --> 01:00:16.008
Oh, no. I can't move over.

01:00:45.538 --> 01:00:48.499
Sir, let me pass.

01:00:48.583 --> 01:00:50.209
Can you move your vehicle?

01:00:52.545 --> 01:00:53.921
What's with him?

01:01:12.899 --> 01:01:15.860
Hey! I said move your car!

01:01:17.028 --> 01:01:18.946
It seems like you're not from around here.

01:01:19.030 --> 01:01:21.073
But here, we have things called rules.

01:01:21.157 --> 01:01:22.408
This is a one-way street.

01:01:22.492 --> 01:01:25.328
I've come much further in.
I have the right of way.

01:01:25.411 --> 01:01:26.537
This is the way out.

01:01:28.247 --> 01:01:31.542
Whoever can back up faster should move.
Can't you see this?

01:01:32.335 --> 01:01:34.128
Tractors can't reverse.

01:01:34.212 --> 01:01:37.006
How can tractors not reverse?
Don't be ridiculous.

01:01:37.089 --> 01:01:38.633
I'm not being ridiculous.

01:01:38.716 --> 01:01:41.052
This tractor can't reverse
because it fell into a ditch.

01:01:43.429 --> 01:01:44.597
Because it fell into a ditch?

01:01:45.807 --> 01:01:47.850
Then, this convertible
can't reverse either

01:01:47.934 --> 01:01:48.935
because that's uncool!

01:02:25.721 --> 01:02:29.433
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:02:29.517 --> 01:02:35.439
THANKS TO SPECIAL GUEST PARK JI-HWAN

01:02:59.881 --> 01:03:01.215
What happened to your ear?

01:03:01.299 --> 01:03:03.843
If you keep loitering,
I'll report you for obstructing business.

01:03:03.926 --> 01:03:04.802
That tractor!

01:03:04.886 --> 01:03:07.597
You're not putting her in charge
of cosmetics again, are you?

01:03:07.680 --> 01:03:11.183
I'm Dam Ye-jin. I don't back out
once I've made up my mind.

01:03:11.267 --> 01:03:12.852
Darling! Hurry and grab the chickens.

01:03:13.811 --> 01:03:14.645
Hey, Changsik!

01:03:14.729 --> 01:03:16.772
-Why did you come here?
-I'm here for one thing.

01:03:16.856 --> 01:03:18.065
Make an official appointment.

01:03:18.149 --> 01:03:20.401
Instead of that, I'll do it my way.

01:03:20.484 --> 01:03:22.528
Is this the way you were talking about?

01:03:22.612 --> 01:03:23.738
My goodness!

01:03:26.991 --> 01:03:28.075
What's your deal?

01:03:28.159 --> 01:03:28.993
Excuse me.

01:03:30.620 --> 01:03:31.454
Thank you.

01:03:42.840 --> 01:03:44.842
Subtitle translation by: Juyoung Park